      "math_academy_id": "q-89612",
      "sequence_position": 2,
      "problem": "Given that the random variable $X$ has the cumulative distribution function\n\n$$\nF(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}0, & x<0 \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{25}, & 0\\le x\\le 5 \\\\ 1, & x>5,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nfind $P(1\\le X\\le 3).$",
      "worked_solution": "Remember that for continuous random variables, it doesn't matter whether or not we include the endpoints of the interval. So we can perform the computation as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(1\\le X\\le 3) & =P(1<X\\le 3) \\\\  & =P(X\\le 3)-P(X\\le 1) \\\\  & =F(3)-F(1) \\\\  & =\\frac{{3}^{2}}{25}-\\frac{{1}^{2}}{25} \\\\  & =\\frac{8}{25}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "answer_fields_complete": true,
